  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-04T01:41:29.445Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, fallback avatars are a completely different avatar that you have to select globally, similar to Quest fallbacks. There is currently no way to upload a \"fallback\" version of a specific avatar on an individual basis, and have it automatically be used when you are performance blocked.\nThis results in weird scenarios, where you see yourself as Avatar A, another person sees you as Avatar B, and yet another person might see you as Avatar C, as in this crude diagram: https://i.imgur.com/gk24OXV.png.\nI propose that we should have the ability to upload a \"fallback\" version of an avatar on the same ID as an existing avatar. When the avatar is performance-blocked, it will first try to use the one uploaded on the same ID. This allows you to have \"lighter\" versions of your avatars for when you are performance-blocked, and would make performance-blocked avatars more consistent.",
